---
import { APP_NAME, APP_DESCRIPTION } from '@/config';
import assets from '@/pwa/assets.json';
import '@/styles/global.css';

/**
 * Privacy policy.
 *
 * Required by both stores before review, and it has to match the Data Safety /
 * App Privacy answers exactly. Shipped as a page inside the app rather than
 * hosted elsewhere so it is covered by the same offline guarantee and cannot
 * rot at a dead link during review.
 *
 * Everything below is a description of what the code actually does. There is a
 * test asserting the app contains no fetch, socket, remote host or webfont, so
 * "sends nothing anywhere" is enforced rather than promised.
 */
const v = assets.version;
const updated = '15 August 2026';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>Privacy · {APP_NAME}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={`How ${APP_NAME} handles your data. It does not collect any.`} />
    <link rel="icon" href={`/favicon.svg?v=${v}`} type="image/svg+xml" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#000000" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#ffffff" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="screen" style="justify-content: flex-start">
      <header class="topbar">
        <a class="topbar__back" href="/"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span><span>Back to the game</span></a>
        <span class="topbar__status"><span>Privacy</span></span>
      </header>

      <div class="screen__body stack stack--6" style="padding-bottom: 3rem">
        <div class="stack stack--3">
          <p class="eyebrow">Last updated {updated}</p>
          <h1 class="display display--md">We don't collect anything</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            {APP_NAME} has no account, no server and no analytics. Nothing you type or say in this game leaves
            your device, because there is nowhere for it to go.
          </p>
        </div>

        <section class="stack stack--3">
          <h2 class="award__title">What we collect</h2>
          <p class="consent__body">
            Nothing. No personal data, no usage data, no identifiers, no advertising IDs, no crash reports,
            no location. We do not use cookies, and there is no tracking of any kind.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="stack stack--3">
          <h2 class="award__title">What stays on your device</h2>
          <p class="consent__body">
            So a game survives an accidental refresh, the app saves the current session in your browser's
            local storage. That save contains only game mechanics: the player names you typed, turn counters,
            scores, and the id numbers of the prompt cards drawn.
          </p>
          <p class="consent__body">
            <b>Answers are never recorded.</b> What anybody actually says in response to a question is not
            stored, transmitted or retained anywhere — not on the device, not by us. Saved games expire after
            12 hours and are deleted when a game finishes. Clearing your browser data removes them
            immediately.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="stack stack--3">
          <h2 class="award__title">What we never ask for</h2>
          <p class="consent__body">
            The app requests no permissions: no camera, no microphone, no location, no contacts, no photos,
            no notifications. It also never asks you for a password, an account, a payment method or access
            to any of your other apps. If something ever claims to be {APP_NAME} and asks for those, it is
            not us.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="stack stack--3">
          <h2 class="award__title">Network use</h2>
          <p class="consent__body">
            The app downloads itself once and then works entirely offline, including in airplane mode. After
            that first load it makes no network requests at all. There are no third-party services, no
            content delivery networks, no embedded fonts and no external images.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="stack stack--3">
          <h2 class="award__title">Children</h2>
          <p class="consent__body">
            {APP_NAME} is for adults and is not directed at children. The 18+ mode is a separate deck behind an
            age confirmation, and its content is never reachable from the general game modes.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="stack stack--3">
          <h2 class="award__title">Changes</h2>
          <p class="consent__body">
            If this policy ever changes, the date at the top of this page changes with it. Since the app
            collects nothing, any change would be to clarify rather than to widen what we do.
          </p>
        </section>

        <div class="consent">
          <p class="consent__title">In short</p>
          <p class="consent__body">
            {APP_DESCRIPTION} Nothing you say in it is recorded, and nothing about you is sent anywhere.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
